---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import StatusChip from "../components/StatusChip.astro";
import WardBars from "../components/WardBars.astro";
import CharterSheet from "../components/CharterSheet.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { harnesses, router } from "../data/harnesses";

/**
 * /lineage/ (site-spec §7): the lineage statement, the carry-set, the fork
 * strategy, what upstream has that we lack, and the affiliation line. The
 * upstream project is named only as "the upstream project" or by Amazon's
 * open-source Kiro agent workspace; its marks appear nowhere.
 */
const title = "Lineage: built on Amazon's open-source Kiro workspace";
const description = "Warding derives from Amazon's open-source Kiro agent workspace (Apache-2.0). The NOTICE, what we carry, the fork plan, and what upstream has that we lack.";
const lineage = "Built on Amazon's open-source Kiro agent workspace, published under Apache-2.0 in 2026. Most of the code is theirs; the attribution notice is in NOTICE. Not affiliated with Amazon.";
const nonKiro = harnesses.filter((h) => !h.upstreamMature);
const registryOffered = ""; // ISO date once the registry has been offered upstream; "" renders "planned"
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} h1="Where it comes from" lead={lineage} breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Lineage", href: "/lineage/" }]}>
  <div class="lineage">
    <p class="caption">The attribution notice, verbatim, is <a href={site.links.notice} rel="noopener">NOTICE</a> in the repository. The upstream project is not named on this site beyond that link; its authors are credited there, in the form the licence asks for.</p>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="carry-h">
      <WardBars align="left" />
      <h2 id="carry-h">The carry-set</h2>
      <p class="measure">What is ours is a thin, named set of changes carried on top of the upstream tree. Everything not on this list is upstream's, and we do not fork it.</p>
      <ol class="carry">
        <li>
          <h3>The harness registry, with kiro-cli optional and last</h3>
          <p>One dock, {harnesses.length} runtimes, chosen by preference order or by one setting: {nonKiro.map((h) => h.command).join(", ")}, then kiro-cli. Ten are non-Kiro; five of them the upstream project does not dock, and both of us dock OpenCode. First run never asks for a vendor account with us. <a href="/registry/">The registry</a>, with what is verified on each.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The harness router, for subagents</h3>
          <p>Chat runs the one harness you choose. The {router.name.toLowerCase()} (<code>{router.command}</code>) {router.what} <a href="/verified/#notyet-h">Registered · unverified</a>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Endpoint removal</h3>
          <p>The upstream project's update feed, app catalog and telemetry are off in the default build, and nothing contacts a server of ours. One inherited address remains: the embedding model is fetched on first embedding use from a CDN the upstream codebase shipped with, checked against a pinned hash; point <code>memory.embed_model_url</code> at your own mirror to avoid it. The run that lists every outbound connection is on <a href="/verified/">the verification log</a> as planned.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The brand</h3>
          <p>The name, the seal, the site and the CLI name <code>{site.cli}</code>. Package identifiers stay as their systems spelled them.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The proof pages</h3>
          <p><a href="/verified/">/verified/</a> and <a href="/registry/">/registry/</a>: a checkmark on this site links to a dated row, and a capability without one is written as unverified.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Dawn-expiring approval grants <StatusChip kind="coming" /></h3>
          <p>A grant that lets a class of command run until a clock time, then asks again.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>The Morning Report <StatusChip kind="coming" /></h3>
          <p>What was done, what was asked, what was refused and what was redacted, counted from the audit log.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3><code>{site.cli} switch</code> <StatusChip kind="coming" /></h3>
          <p>Change the docked harness in one command; schedules, memory and channels stay.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="strategy-h">
      <WardBars align="left" />
      <h2 id="strategy-h">The fork strategy</h2>
      <CharterSheet class="strategy">
        <dl class="strategy-list">
          <div><dt>Track upstream</dt><dd>Not a hard fork. Upstream releases are merged, not re-implemented; every one of them is free work for the people running Warding.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Rebase quarterly</dt><dd>The carry-set is rebased onto the upstream tree once a quarter, and we refuse to widen it.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Offer the registry upstream</dt><dd>The harness registry, kiro-cli optional and last, is offered to the upstream project as a change of theirs to accept or decline. {registryOffered ? `Offered on ${registryOffered}.` : "Planned; not offered yet."}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Harden downstream</dt><dd>The proof artefacts and the two mechanisms above are where the work goes.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </CharterSheet>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="lack-h">
      <WardBars align="left" />
      <h2 id="lack-h">What upstream has that we lack</h2>
      <p class="measure">If you use kiro-cli, the upstream project is ahead and we say so. <a href="/compare/upstream/">The comparison</a> puts its strengths first.</p>
      <ul class="lack measure">
        <li>No signed installers yet; upstream ships them for macOS, Windows and Linux.</li>
        <li>No Docker image yet; upstream publishes one.</li>
        <li>No desktop app yet; upstream ships one.</li>
        <li>No KAS yet; upstream docks it. Both of us dock OpenCode.</li>
        <li>On a non-Kiro harness, upstream gives the agent its own MCP tools; Warding passes them only to kiro-cli today, so on other harnesses the agent cannot create jobs, spawn subagents or ask you a question from chat.</li>
        <li>Install polish, generally. The upstream project is at a later version with more hands on it.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block" aria-labelledby="aff-h">
      <WardBars align="left" />
      <h2 id="aff-h">Not affiliated</h2>
      <p class="measure">Warding Labs is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Amazon or the upstream project. The upstream name and marks belong to their owners and appear nowhere in this product's name, logo, domain or tagline. Releases of this tree are listed on <a href="/changelog/">the changelog</a>, which reproduces only what we shipped.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .lineage { display: grid; gap: 56px; }
  .block { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .carry { list-style: none; margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 20px; counter-reset: carry; max-width: 76ch; }
  .carry li { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding-left: 56px; position: relative; }
  .carry li::before { counter-increment: carry; content: counter(carry, decimal-leading-zero); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 2px; font-family: var(--font-clock); font-size: 22px; color: var(--lamp); }
  .carry h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .carry p { color: var(--fg-2); }
  .strategy { max-width: 76ch; }
  .strategy-list { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .strategy-list div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .strategy-list dt { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: 1.125rem; }
  .strategy-list dd { margin: 0; color: var(--fg-2); }
  .lack { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25em; display: grid; gap: 8px; color: var(--fg-2); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .strategy-list div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 4px; }
    .carry li { padding-left: 44px; }
  }
</style>
